sson idea.","options":["Calling everything fake without evidence. Analyse features.","News and bias analysis examines news values (timeliness, proximity, conflict), selection of sources and language slant (claimed vs alleged). Bias can be…","Strong answer: Names wording/source choices; avoids claiming secret motives you cannot know.","Careful use of bias with clear evidence."],"question":"Which statement is a common mistake when practising news values?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Understanding is shown by new evidence and named bias, not by copying the model.","options":["Treat a missing detail as a stated fact.","Apply the idea with new evidence and name the bias used.","Repeat the worked example wording with no new evidence.","Choose randomly because any option could be right."],"question":"A learner is practising news values. Which approach best shows understanding?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"The skill is shown by quoting or pointing to wording that carries news values.","options":["Say the writing is good without naming any words.","Calling everything fake without evidence. Analyse features.","Point to exact words in the sentence that show news values and say what they do.","Ignore the sentence and invent a more exciting event."],"question":"Read: \"Beside the oval, Kai practised bowling until the sun slipped low.\" Which choice best uses news values from this lesson?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"The correct statement applies the language skill; the others miss the evidence.","options":["Copy the model word-for-word and call that independent work.","Strong answer: Names wording/source choices; avoids claiming secret motives you cannot know.","Calling everything fake without evidence. Analyse features.","Ignore the words and invent a more exciting event."],"question":"Which statement correctly applies the lesson idea about news values?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"c